# SQL Data Cleaning Project

## Project Overview

This project uses MySQL to clean and prepare a layoffs dataset for analysis. The original dataset was preserved while staging tables were created for the data-cleaning process.

## Data Cleaning Process

- Removed duplicate records
- Standardized company names
- Standardized industry values
- Standardized country values
- Converted the date column to the DATE data type
- Identified null and blank values
- Populated missing industry values where possible
- Removed records without useful layoff information
- Removed unnecessary columns

## SQL Concepts Demonstrated

- SELECT
- WHERE
- UPDATE
- DELETE
- CREATE TABLE
- INSERT
- CTEs
- ROW_NUMBER()
- PARTITION BY
- DISTINCT
- TRIM()
- LIKE
- JOIN
- NULL handling
- ALTER TABLE

## Technologies Used

- SQL
- MySQL
- MySQL Workbench

## Project Outcome

The layoffs dataset was cleaned and standardized to prepare it for further exploratory data analysis.
